[
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "1",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"
  },
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "1",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "The determinant is a scalar value that can be computed from a square matrix. For a 3x3 matrix, the Leibniz formula (or Rule of Sarrus) provides a straightforward way to calculate it."
  },
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "2",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "General 3x3 Matrix"
  },
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "2",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "A = \\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & i \\end{vmatrix}"
  },
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "3",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "The determinant is calculated using the Leibniz formula. For a 3x3 matrix, this is often remembered as:"
  },
  {
    "page": "1",
    "part": "3",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(A) = aei + bfg + cdh - ceg - bdi - afh"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "4",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "Example 1: Calculating the Determinant"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "4",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Calculate the determinant of the following 3x3 matrix:"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "4",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "B = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9 \\end{vmatrix}"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "5",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Identify the elements: a=1, b=2, c=3, d=4, e=5, f=6, g=7, h=8, i=9."
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "5",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Apply the Leibniz formula:"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "5",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(B) = 1\\cdot5\\cdot9 + 2\\cdot6\\cdot7 + 3\\cdot4\\cdot8"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "5",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "- 3\\cdot5\\cdot7 - 2\\cdot4\\cdot9 - 1\\cdot6\\cdot8"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "6",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Now compute each term:"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "6",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(B) = 45 + 84 + 96 - 105 - 72 - 48"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "6",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(B) = 225 - 225 = 0"
  },
  {
    "page": "2",
    "part": "6",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Since det(B) = 0, the matrix is singular (not invertible)."
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "7",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "Example 2: Another Determinant Calculation"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "7",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Calculate the determinant of this 3x3 matrix:"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "7",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "C = \\begin{vmatrix} 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "8",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Identify the elements: a=2, b=0, c=1, d=-1, e=3, f=2, g=4, h=-2, i=1."
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "8",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Apply the Leibniz formula:"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "8",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(C) = 2\\cdot3\\cdot1 + 0\\cdot2\\cdot4 + 1\\cdot(-1)\\cdot(-2)"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "8",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "- 1\\cdot3\\cdot4 - 0\\cdot(-1)\\cdot1 - 2\\cdot2\\cdot(-2)"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "9",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Now compute each term carefully:"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "9",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(C) = 6 + 0 + 2 - 12 - 0 - (-8)"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "9",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(C) = 8 - 12 + 8 = 4"
  },
  {
    "page": "3",
    "part": "9",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Since det(C) = 4 ≠ 0, the matrix is invertible."
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "10",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "Leibniz Formula - Visual Trick"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "10",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "A helpful visual trick for the 3x3 determinant (Rule of Sarrus) is to repeat the first two columns:"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "10",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\begin{array}{ccc|cc} a & b & c & a & b \\\\ d & e & f & d & e \\\\ g & h & i & g & h \\end{array}"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Sum the products of the three diagonals going down-right:"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\text{Down-right: } aei + bfg + cdh"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Sum the products of the three diagonals going down-left:"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\text{Down-left: } ceg + bdi + afh"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Subtract the second sum from the first:"
  },
  {
    "page": "4",
    "part": "11",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(A) = (aei + bfg + cdh) - (ceg + bdi + afh)"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "12",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "Example 3: Using the Visual Trick"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "12",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Find the determinant using the visual trick:"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "12",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "D = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 \\end{vmatrix}"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "13",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Repeat the first two columns:"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "13",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\begin{array}{ccc|cc} 1 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\end{array}"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "14",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Products down-right:"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "14",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "1\\cdot1\\cdot0 = 0 \\quad 2\\cdot4\\cdot5 = 40 \\quad 3\\cdot0\\cdot6 = 0"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "14",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\text{Sum} = 0 + 40 + 0 = 40"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "15",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Products down-left:"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "15",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "3\\cdot1\\cdot5 = 15 \\quad 2\\cdot4\\cdot6 = 48 \\quad 1\\cdot0\\cdot0 = 0"
  },
  {
    "page": "5",
    "part": "15",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\text{Sum} = 15 + 48 + 0 = 63"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "16",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "Finally, subtract the sums:"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "16",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det(D) = 40 - 63 = -23"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "16",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "The determinant is -23, so the matrix is invertible."
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "17",
    "typ": "title",
    "content": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "17",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "For a 3x3 matrix, the Leibniz formula provides a systematic way to compute the determinant:"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "17",
    "typ": "katex",
    "content": "\\det\\begin{vmatrix} a&b&c\\\\d&e&f\\\\g&h&i \\end{vmatrix} = aei + bfg + cdh - ceg - bdi - afh"
  },
  {
    "page": "6",
    "part": "17",
    "typ": "text",
    "content": "If det(A) = 0, the matrix is singular. If det(A) ≠ 0, the matrix is invertible."
  }
]